\ Star Raiders on telic's drawing words, keyboard and synthesizer.
\
\   ./telic examples/star-raiders.telic
\
\ The Zylons hold the galaxy's 16 by 8 sectors and close in on the
\ starbases; a starbase with Zylon ships north, east, south and west of it
\ falls a minute later. Hyperwarp from sector to sector on the Galactic
\ Chart, keeping the target marker on the crosshairs as it veers, fight the
\ fighters, cruisers and basestars you find there, and dock at a starbase to
\ refuel and repair. The mission ends when the last Zylon ship is destroyed,
\ the energy runs out, or the ship is destroyed with its shields down, and
\ the score gives a rank from Galactic Cook to Star Commander.
\
\ Keys: the arrows steer (up lifts the nose), space fires, 0-9 set the
\ speed, F front view, A aft view, L long-range scan, G Galactic Chart,
\ S shields, C attack computer, T tracking computer, H hyperwarp, M the other
\ Zylon ship, P pause, backspace aborts the mission, escape quits. On the
\ title screen return starts the mission and tab changes it.
\
\ A gamepad works too: the left stick steers (up lifts the nose), A or the
\ right trigger fires, d-pad up and down change the speed, X the front view
\ and pressed again the aft view, Y the Galactic Chart and the left shoulder
\ the long-range scan (each pressed again for the front view), B hyperwarp, back the shields, the left stick's
\ button the attack computer, the right stick's the tracking computer, the
\ right shoulder the other Zylon ship, start pauses. On the title screen
\ start begins the mission and back changes it.
\
\ The rules and numbers, and their source, are in
\ examples/starraiders/universe.telic; the flight in flight.telic; the
\ picture and the sound in screen.telic.

"starraiders/universe.telic" load
"starraiders/flight.telic" load
"starraiders/screen.telic" load

\ the keys outside the cockpit: in the demonstration return starts the
\ mission and tab changes it; in a mission P pauses and the cockpit keys act
: read-control-keys ( -- )
	:demo game@ if
		:return key-pressed? :start pad-pressed? or if :mission game@ 0 new-game exit then
		:tab key-pressed? :back pad-pressed? or if
			:mission game@ 1+ 4 mod 1 new-game
			[ "NOVICE MISSION" "PILOT MISSION" "WARRIOR MISSION" "COMMANDER MISSION" ] :mission game@ @i 1 array-of say
		then
		exit
	then
	:p key-pressed? :start pad-pressed? or if :paused game@ 0= :paused game! then
	:paused game@ 0= if read-keys then ;

\ one screen frame: the keys, the game loops due, the sound, the picture
: frame ( elapsed -- )
	| elapsed |
	:escape key-pressed? if 0 :running game! exit then
	run-due-events
	read-control-keys
	:paused game@ 0= if elapsed run-loops then
	play-cues
	update-engine-sound
	draw ;

\ run the game until escape, each frame advanced by the measured time since the last, at most 1/20 s
: play ( -- )
	audio-on
	settle-effects
	1 :running game!
	0 1 new-game
	:c3 1 :engines note-on
	now to last
	begin :running game@ while
		now to moment
		moment last - 0.05 min2 to elapsed
		moment to last
		elapsed ' frame screen-frame
	repeat
	silence-audio
	audio-off ;

play
